Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: contrib/pds/tif_pdsdirwrite.c
Line: 795
Function: TIFFWriteAnyArray
Bug type: null-pointer-dereference
CWE: CWE-476
Explanation: When n * TIFFDataWidth(type) exceeds the small stack buffer, w is allocated with _TIFFmalloc() but not checked. On allocation failure (e.g., large n), w remains NULL and is dereferenced in the per-type loops (e.g., bp[i] = ...), causing a NULL pointer dereference.

